          "value": "Watt (W)",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Simple Machine Types",
          "value": "6 Types",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Mechanical Advantage Formula",
          "value": "Load / Effort",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "hk9nkm9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vw06g1k",
      "content": "Mechanical concepts form the basic foundation of engineering and technical trades. Understanding concepts such as force, work, energy, power, machines, and friction helps workers understand how machines operate and how mechanical systems perform work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "23uayx2",
      "content": "These principles are widely used in mechanical engineering, automobile repair, manufacturing, construction, and maintenance work."
    },
    {
      "id": "lkv5228",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Force"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "olac3dx",
      "content": "Force is a push or pull acting on a body that can change its state of motion or shape. It is measured in Newtons (N)."
    },
