    {
      "id": "m0zdnt6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Work"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iom12uk",
      "content": "Work is said to be done when a force moves an object through a distance. The unit of work is Joule (J)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gtlsin8",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o733d5s",
      "content": "Work = Force × Distance"
    },
    {
      "id": "ovjuxqi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jujerxv",
      "content": "Energy is the capacity to do work. It exists in different forms."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Mechanical Advantage is the ratio of the output force produced by a machine to the input force applied to it.",
      "id": "0ga5gco"
    },
