      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Mechanical Advantage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "urk69hs",
      "content": "Mechanical Advantage (MA) is the ratio of output force to input force in a machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u7pvdrm",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8lpkcmb",
      "content": "Mechanical Advantage = Load ÷ Effort"
    },
    {
      "id": "jq3mnlk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Friction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3texso5",
      "content": "Friction is the force that opposes the motion of objects when they come into contact."
    },
